## HOLDS
No Jira write outside the closed list; no transition of any key; no touch of any other ticket; no statement that anything is built, deployed, drafted, proposed, sent or removed that a record or a GitHub read does not show; **no sentence that a change is on a host except as the deploy record's own words, RELAYED and dated; and no sentence that a further deploy is planned, ruled or approved**; **no ruling put in anyone's mouth beyond the option's own words: every reading (that the hosted showcase is the MPS demo, that the 10:25 ruling covers this deploy only, what the board notes mean) is the coordinator's and is written as such**; no person's name and no card id in any Jira text or record line. If a post, create, commit or merge fails or reads back unequal: stop that item, fix the root cause, re-verify; never retry blindly. **Shell:** no `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths (`!` and a space are in the project path); `git -C '...' --no-optional-locks` for reads; `python3 -I -B`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; never `echo ====` (use `echo ----`); never name a shell variable `path`; a `gh api` URL holding `?` is quoted; `cp` into `.tools/b1611/` only (a write into another seat's tree is refused by a hook: read with `cat`). **Standing lines:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (above); no message to any human; Jira writes only where this kit's scope says so; never delete (quarantine); never print a credential; `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP. **MPS hosted is card per deploy; you deploy nothing, and no text says the pass did.**

